# Arrow functions

Write functions as arrow functions, including components, helpers, and callbacks.

```tsx
// Bad
export default function RecipesPage() {
  return <h1>Recipes</h1>;
}

async function loadRecipes() {
  return db.select().from(recipesTable);
}

// Good
const RecipesPage = () => {
  return <h1>Recipes</h1>;
};

export default RecipesPage;

const loadRecipes = async () => {
  return db.select().from(recipesTable);
};
```

Use a `function` declaration only when an arrow function cannot express it, such as a generator (`function*`).
